Built from the unmodified upstream checkout with Node.js 24.14.1, npm 11.11.0,
JDK 17.0.20.1, Android SDK platform 37.0 and build-tools 37.0.0.
The repository's Gradle wrapper pins Gradle 9.6.1 and verifies its checksum.

Rebuild in a separate source checkout:
    git clone https://github.com/GrapheneOS/PdfViewer
    cd PdfViewer
    git checkout bbe049314d8c29b7554587bf39efde67cc9f0e03
    npm ci
    JAVA_HOME=/path/to/jdk17 ANDROID_HOME=/path/to/android-sdk ./gradlew --no-daemon assembleRelease
    npm test

Copy app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release-unsigned.apk here.
Do not provide keystore.properties; this prebuilt is intentionally unsigned.
Soong uses the product's default development certificate, matching ESpeakNG's
existing convention. The normal CharaROM release-signing flow must map this
certificate to the ROM release key. Do not use PRESIGNED or the platform key.

The app requests no dangerous or network permissions and registers an
application/pdf VIEW intent filter. AndroidX adds an app-private signature
permission for non-exported receivers. No default-handler or permission XML
is needed for this swap.
MIT LICENSE and Apache-2.0 PDFJS_LICENSE are copied unchanged from upstream.

